defects.root_cause:
The bars are numeric, but their meaning is hidden. DimensionBar splits one track in proportion to score_a/(score_a+score_b) (SmartCompareApp/src/components/primitives/DimensionBar.tsx:49-51). It is fed scoring_v2.dimensions[i].score_a/score_b (ResultsContent.tsx:460-497). The numbers are deliberately hidden (DimensionBars.tsx:345-361 scoreHookHidden), and no unit, scale or source is shown. Each score is a 0-100 composite of a generic signal (see MYEZ-008):
- spec signals are pair-relative in a dampened 45-85 band, with 65 for a tie (scoring_service.py:2472-2541);
- ratings map to 20-100 (:2544-2551);
- reliability/popularity are raw x100 (:2553-2558);
- a missing side is the sentinel MISSING_SCORE=50 (:2491-2492, :2548-2549, :2556-2557). Only both-sided-missing dims are omitted (:3570-3572); a one-sided-missing dim ships the 50 and renders as a bar.

Every category dim gets a hard-coded confidence 'medium' (:3585), so the low-confidence opacity and '≈' cue never fire. The backend sets winner=None for ties, low confidence and one-sided-missing dims (_dim_winner :3192-3237). The client then falls back to a score heuristic and still paints one side emerald, ties going to the overall winner (DimensionBars.tsx:263-269). The 'no false certainty' Decision B is therefore lost visually. Captions are qualitative constants independent of data: 'More distinctive', 'Longer-lasting', 'Stronger projection', 'Comparable' for a margin under 1 (scoring_service.py:3608-3687). Otherwise they read '+Npt <label>', which the client swaps back to the dim label (_deltaText.ts:43-47; DimensionBars.tsx:287-288). So the caption under a bar often just repeats its name (V07 'الحرفية' under 'الحرفية'). When no rating exists, fragrance 'Character' and 'Longevity' are the same number, because spec_secondary falls back to spec (:2340-2352; the client fixture DimensionBars.test.tsx:140-141 shows identical 74.1/55.9).
